---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/site';
const interests = ['AI voice agents', 'Customer communication', 'Workflow automation', 'SaaS products', 'Client services to repeatable software'];
---
<Base title="About Fazle Bary Nayem | Background and Approach" description="Learn about Nayem's background in software, AI automation, and business, and the experience shaping his work as a founder.">
  <PageHero index="About" eyebrow="Fazle Bary Nayem" title="One company delivers. Two products scale it. <em>Each makes the other better.</em>" lead="Client work shows us where businesses lose time. Products are how we fix it for more than one business at a time. That loop is the whole idea." />
  <section class="loop-sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="loop">
        <li class="reveal"><span class="label">01 / Deliver</span><p>Abedin Tech builds AI, automation and software inside client businesses.</p></li>
        <li class="reveal"><span class="label">02 / Notice</span><p>The same problems show up again and again: missed calls, slow follow-up, inconsistent content.</p></li>
        <li class="reveal"><span class="label">03 / Productise</span><p>Callinva and SaleAnto turn those fixes into products any business can use.</p></li>
        <li class="reveal"><span class="label">04 / Return</span><p>What the products learn makes the next client project faster and better.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="photo-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Portrait name="working" alt="Fazle Bary Nayem at work" ratio="16 / 7" caption="At work with the Abedin Tech team" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split-2">
      <aside class="sticky reveal">
        <div class="facts">
          <dl class="dl">
            <div><dt>Name</dt><dd>{profile.name}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>{profile.primaryRole}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Building</dt><dd>Callinva and SaleAnto</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Bangladesh</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Works with</dt><dd>Businesses in the US, UK and beyond</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p class="lead" style="color:var(--ink);max-width:none">A useful product has to work for two people at once: the person using it, and the business paying for it. Everything here starts from that.</p>
        <p>My experience brings together software development, AI automation, digital marketing, product thinking, and the everyday work of running a business. I care about how these areas connect, because a useful product needs to work for both the people using it and the business behind it.</p>

        <h2>From client work to products</h2>
        <p>Through Abedin Tech, I work with a team delivering websites, software, automation, and digital growth projects. That work has given me a practical view of how businesses find customers, manage operations, and use technology.</p>
        <p>It has also shaped my interest in building products. When a problem appears across different businesses, I want to understand whether it can be solved in a way that more people can use.</p>
        <p>Today, that includes Callinva, focused on AI calling and customer communication, and SaleAnto, focused on social content creation and scheduling. These products reflect different parts of the same interest: making business workflows easier to manage.</p>

        <h2>How I approach the work</h2>
        <p>I like to start with the problem and ask what a useful result would look like. From there, the work is a cycle of building, testing, listening, and improving. I value clear communication, practical design, and attention to the details that affect real users.</p>
        <p>I also believe good systems should make room for people. Automation should have clear boundaries, reliable information, and an easy path to human support when needed.</p>

        <h2>What I am focused on</h2>
        <ul class="chips">{interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>I share lessons from this work through the <a href="/insights/">Insights</a> section.</p>
        <p>Building from Bangladesh gives me a strong connection to local talent and an international perspective on the businesses we serve. I want to keep creating opportunities for useful technology and capable people to reach a wider market.</p>

        <h2>Short biography</h2>
        <blockquote>{profile.shortBio}</blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand eyebrow="Work together" title="Want a build partner who <em>ships products?</em>" body="If you are working on a product, a business problem or a partnership that fits this work, send a short note with some context." label="Start a conversation" />
</Base>

<style>
  .loop-sec { padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px); }
  .loop { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0 32px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr)); counter-reset: l; }
  .loop li { position: relative; padding: 22px 0 8px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .loop li:first-child { border-top-color: var(--red); }
  .loop p { margin: 12px 0 0; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.3; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 48; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) { .loop li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '\2192'; position: absolute; right: -24px; top: 14px; color: var(--red); } }
  .photo-band { padding-top: 0; }
  .chips { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.4em; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 10px; }
  .chips li { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 22px; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 48, 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1; }
  .chips li:not(:last-child)::after { content: ','; }
  blockquote { margin: 0; padding: 4px 0 4px 28px; border-left: 2px solid var(--red); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-2); font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 48; }
</style>
